## Modules by Phase

### Governance module — launch requirement
- `GovernanceToken` (`ERC20Votes`): token + delegation support for **protocol**
  governance only. `[MVP]`
- Seed distribution to early protocol participants / treasury. `[MVP]`
- `Timelock` (`TimelockController`) owned by team multisig at launch. `[MVP]`
- `CryptoWatcherGovernor`: proposals for protocol params (reviewer roster changes,
  methodology version, review fees, backend submitter rotation). Voting delay/period,
  quorum fraction and a **non-zero proposal threshold** (anti-spam) are constructor
  parameters and remain governance-tunable via the OZ setters. `[MVP]`
- `ProtocolSettings`: Timelock-owned `methodologyVersion`. This value is **read by
  every `ProjectReview` at publish time** and stamped onto each report, so governance
  changes have direct on-chain effect (no orphaned settings). `[MVP]`
- Community token-weighted **protocol** proposals, quorum + voting delay. `[Phase 1]`
- Vote delegation UX support for protocol votes. `[Phase 2]`
- Full DAO: treasury + upgrade control governed on-chain. `[Final]`

### Review registry module (folder: `review/`)
- `ProjectWatcherFactory`: backend-controlled `submitProject(projectId, submitter)`
  callable only by the platform `backend` (users pay for their review off-chain;
  the backend then emits the on-chain record on their behalf). Deploys one
  `ProjectReview` per project, records the paying user as submitter, prevents
  duplicate ids and exposes a registry (`reviewOf`, `submitterOf`, enumeration).
  `Ownable2Step` + `Pausable`; governance owns it, can rotate the `backend`
  address (`setBackend`) and pause submissions. `[MVP]`
- `ProjectReview`: governor-only score publication with an immutable on-chain audit
  trail. Lifecycle `Requested → InAnalysis → Published`; the team/operator advances
  analysis, then vetted council governors call `publishReport(riskScore, reportHash)`.
  Each report is stamped with the current `methodologyVersion`; re-reviews append a
  new immutable round. A governor cannot review a project they submitted
  (conflict-of-interest guard). No public vote-to-rate. `[MVP]`
- Indexer-friendly events (`ProjectSubmitted`, `AnalysisStarted`, `ReportPublished`)
  carrying score, governor, round, report hash and methodology version. `[MVP]`
- Governor-gated score publication (only council members eligible in
  `ReputationRegistry`, also granted `GOVERNOR_ROLE`). `[MVP]`
- Multi-chain deployment of project registry contracts. `[Phase 2]`

### Reputation module (council governor credentials)
- `ReputationRegistry`: governor allow-list + accountability weight for **council
  members only** — not public score voting eligibility. Eligible governors are also
  granted `GOVERNOR_ROLE`. `[MVP→Phase 1]`
- Multi-factor reviewer reputation (report quality, timeliness, appeal overturn rate,
  conflict disclosures). `[Phase 1]`
- On-chain reviewer credential references. `[Phase 2]`
- Decentralized expertise verification. `[Final]`

### Rewards module (reviewer compensation)
- `RewardDistributor`: compensate governors for completed reviews; penalties for
  misconduct — **not** rewards for public project score voting. `[Phase 1]`
- Slashing / penalties for governor misconduct (conflicts, falsified reports). `[Phase 1]`
- Sustainable reviewer compensation + treasury funding. `[Final]`

## Scoring

- Official project score published by governor council; methodology version referenced
  on-chain. `[MVP]`
- Score factors enriched with external risk signals to **assist** governors (human-in-the-loop). `[Phase 3]`
- Appeals and re-review workflow (governor council, not token vote). `[Phase 1]`

## Security posture

- **Access control.** Report publication is gated to vetted council governors
  (`ReputationRegistry.isEligible` + `GOVERNOR_ROLE`); lifecycle transitions are
  `team`-only; the factory is `Ownable2Step` + `Pausable` and backend-gated.
- **Governance wiring.** `ProtocolSettings.methodologyVersion` is consumed by every
  `ProjectReview`, so governed parameters have real on-chain effect. The governor
  ships with a non-zero `proposalThreshold` to prevent proposal spam.
- **Deploy hardening.** `Deploy.s.sol` hands timelock control to the governor and
  renounces the deployer's `DEFAULT_ADMIN_ROLE`, and delegates the deployer's votes
  so governance is immediately usable. Pinned compiler pragma (`0.8.26`).
- **Conflict of interest.** A governor cannot publish a report for a project they
  submitted; risk scores are bounded `[0, 100]` and report hashes must be non-zero.
- **Known trust assumptions.** The `backend` submitter and the governor council are
  trusted, governance-rotatable roles; the full token supply is minted to the
  deployer at genesis and **must be distributed to the treasury/council before
  mainnet** so a single key cannot dominate governance.

## Security & Testing

- Foundry unit + fuzz tests per module, CI security scanning. `[MVP]`
- Fork-based integration tests in `test/integration/` exercise the full deploy +
  governance + review-registry lifecycle against a Sepolia fork (`SEPOLIA_RPC_URL`); they
  skip automatically when no RPC is configured. `[MVP]`
- External audits scaling with phase. `[Phase 2 → Final]`
- Formal verification of core contracts. `[Final]`

## Conventions

- One module = one folder under `src/`, with matching `test/` and `script/` folders.
- Interfaces live in each module's `interfaces/` folder.
- Deployed addresses tracked per chain in `deployments/`.
- Use `AccessControl` roles (from `access/Roles.sol`) instead of bare `onlyOwner`.
- Format Solidity with `forge fmt`; repo-level `pnpm run format` runs Prettier for
  TypeScript/React docs and `forge fmt` for contracts. `[MVP]`
